# M0 -- content fidelity.
#
# One implementation commits a corpus into a mode, the other commits the same
# corpus into the same mode, and the commit checksums are compared. Object
# identity is independent of repository mode, so a disagreement names the corpus
# feature that diverged.
#
# Both implementations run in the same environment, so a corpus that records the
# invoking user's ids compares validly without canonical ownership.
#
# Field reference and the outcome vocabulary are in README.md.

family: M0
corpus: C0 C1 C2 C3 C4 C5 C6 C7 C8 C9 C10 C11 C12 C13
modes: bare-split-xattrs
tier: T0
outcome: refused-both
severity: interop
identity: n-a
oracle: exit-status stderr-text
evidence: -
spec: format-reference.md#repository-modes-and-on-disk-storage
question: Record both refusal texts. The tool answers "Not allowed due to repo
 mode" for every write. Confirm the port refuses when the transaction opens
 rather than failing later in the write.
note: The tool's write support for this mode is gated and incomplete, and the
 port does not write it. Read-side interoperability for a repository the tool
 produced is covered in m1-operate.matrix.

